      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 1 at 3:32AM HST until November 2 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI AND OAHU...\n...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH FACING SHORES OF\nMOLOKAI AND MAUI...\n\n.A moderate, long-period northwest (330 degrees) swell will build\nrapidly to a peak this morning. Advisory level surf is expected\nfor north and west facing shores exposed to the swell, with high\nsurf expected to continue into Monday. The swell may shift to a\nslightly more northerly direction for a brief time Monday, before\ndeclining Tuesday.\n\n* WHAT...For north facing shores, building to 15 to 20 feet. For\nwest facing shores, building to 10 to 15 feet.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai and Oahu,\nand north facing shores of Molokai and Maui.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM HST Monday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
      "areaDesc": "Niihau; Kauai Southwest; Waianae Coast; Oahu North Shore; Maui Windward West; Kauai North; Kauai East; Koolau Windward; Molokai Windward; Molokai North; Maui Central Valley North; Windward Haleakala",
